„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙRor a charmer, or a consulter with familiar spirits, or a wizard, or a necromancer.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ—For all that do these things are an abomination unto the LORD: and because of these abominations the LORD thy God doth drive them out from before thee.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ,Thou shalt be perfect with the LORD thy God.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¥For these nations, which thou shalt possess, hearkened unto observers of times, and unto diviners: but as for thee, the LORD thy God hath not suffered thee so to do.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ„The LORD thy God will raise up unto thee a Prophet from the midst of thee, of thy brethren, like unto me; unto him ye shall hearken;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÖaccording to all that thou desiredst of the LORD thy God in Horeb in the day of the assembly, saying, Let me not hear again the voice of the LORD my God, neither let me see this great fire any more, that I die not.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙMAnd the LORD said unto me, They have well spoken that which they have spoken.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¨I will raise them up a Prophet from among their brethren, like unto thee, and will put my words in his mouth; and he shall speak unto them all that I shall command him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙƒAnd it shall come to pass, that whosoever will not hearken unto my words which he shall speak in my name, I will require it of him.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙµBut the prophet, which shall presume to speak a word in my name, which I have not commanded him to speak, or that shall speak in the name of other gods, even that prophet shall die.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙZAnd if thou say in thine heart, How shall we know the word which the LORD hath not spoken?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙİWhen a prophet speaketh in the name of the LORD, if the thing follow not, nor come to pass, that is the thing which the LORD hath not spoken, but the prophet hath spoken it presumptuously: thou shalt not be afraid of him.¦layout ªlast_verse